  message: "Second outside-reader review, 2026-11-13 (self-run cache f36c63310c791188/results/c872eb7a7e793eab/ac34c56c06ec1788, re-checked on dev fed15705d7, 20 other repositories measured; ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/outside_reader_review2_11142026). THE STATEMENT REPRODUCES on dev fed15705d7: the first line of the self-run sketch ends '> Requires Python 3.10+.', this item's own sample string. The 2026-07-11 fix is in _extract_readme_description_heuristic only; sketch_embeddings.extract_readme_description_embedding, which runs first whenever sentence-transformers is installed, has no such rule (called directly on this repository's README it returns the description followed by three blockquotes). knex shows the opposite case: its one-line description is itself a blockquote, which the heuristic's skip rule would drop. Filed as WI-monuf-jikar-tumip-zokab-loviz-mubos-sofuv-dorav. This item's status is left as it is; reopening it or leaving the work to the new item is the owner's call."  # 8665
